<!-- ============================================================
     Check Point SmartConsole CVE-2026-16232 Improper Authentication
     MITRE ATT&CK Techniques:
       T1190  - Exploit Public-Facing Application (TA0001 Initial Access)
       T1078  - Valid Accounts: use of obtained token (TA0001/TA0005)
       T1098  - Account Manipulation: admin account creation post-bypass (TA0003)
       T1562.004 - Impair Defenses: Disable or Modify System Firewall (TA0005)
     Rule IDs: 104152-104159
     Author: SecOps Engineer (Purple Team, ESKA-632)
     Date: 2026-07-23

     Vulnerability Summary:

     CVE-2026-16232 is an improper authentication vulnerability in Check Point
     SmartConsole, the primary management application for Check Point Security
     Gateways. An unauthenticated remote attacker can send a specially crafted
     request to the SmartConsole management API and obtain a valid application
     login token without providing legitimate credentials. The attacker can then
     use the token to authenticate with full administrative privileges and
     manage the connected Security Gateway (modify firewall policy, install
     rules, create admin accounts, pivot to managed gateways).

     CISA KEV added 2026-07-22. Federal deadline 2026-07-25 (BOD 26-04).
     CVSS score: Critical. Exploitation is expected to be straightforward and
     will likely be incorporated into ransomware pre-positioning toolkits.

     Attack Flow:

     1. Attacker probes SmartConsole management API (/web_api/ endpoint,
        typically TCP 443 or 19009 on the Smart Management Server).
     2. Crafted unauthenticated request to /web_api/login (or equivalent
        token issuance endpoint) exploits the improper auth flaw.
     3. Server returns a valid session token (sid) without credential check.
     4. Attacker uses the token to call privileged API methods:
        - /web_api/publish (commit policy changes)
        - /web_api/install-policy (push rules to gateways)
        - /web_api/add-administrator (create backdoor admin)
        - /web_api/set-access-rule (add permissive firewall rules)

     Detection Approach:

     1. (104152) Base anchor: SmartConsole API login events from any source.
        Level 5 - correlation anchor, not a standalone alert.
     2. (104153) Login success from source with recent failed attempts (bypass
        pattern: CVE-2026-16232 may not produce visible failures, but scanners
        often probe before exploiting). Level 12.
     3. (104154) Rapid login attempts from the same source (brute-force or
        automated exploit tool probing the token endpoint). Level 12 frequency.
     4. (104155) API authentication failure spike: multiple 401 responses
        from the same source (pre-bypass reconnaissance). Level 11 frequency.
     5. (104156) Privileged policy operation (install-policy, publish) logged
        immediately after fresh SmartConsole login. Level 14.
     6. (104157) Admin account creation via SmartConsole API (persistence
        post-bypass: add-administrator or set-administrator). Level 14.
     7. (104158) Off-hours SmartConsole management API authentication.
        Level 9 - behavioral anomaly, correlate with other indicators.
     8. (104159) Firewall policy modification (add or delete access rule) via
        SmartConsole API - high-confidence post-exploitation pivot. Level 13.

     Log Source Prerequisites:

     These rules target syslog from the Check Point Smart Management Server.
     Process names present in the logs: api_server, cpmad, mgmtd, cpwmd, cpsmd.
     If the management server is not in the environment, rules are precautionary
     and will not fire. Deploy now so coverage is in place if a Check Point
     management server is onboarded or network traffic from one is observed.

     For richer field extraction (srcip, username, session id), deploy a
     Check Point syslog decoder if available. Rules are written to trigger
     on log message content alone (no dedicated decoder required).

     References:
       - CISA KEV 2026-07-22: CVE-2026-16232
       - Check Point advisory (expected sk###### to be published)
       - CVSS Critical - unauthenticated remote token acquisition
     ============================================================ -->

<group name="checkpoint,smartconsole,initial_access,cve_2026_16232,">

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1190  - SmartConsole API login anchor (correlation base)
       Rule ID: 104152
       Matches any SmartConsole management API authentication event
       (success or failure) from api_server or cpmad syslog.
       Level 5 - informational anchor used by frequency rules below.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="104152" level="5">
    <program_name>^(api_server|cpmad|mgmtd|cpwmd|cpsmd)$</program_name>
    <regex type="pcre2">(?i)(smartconsole\s+(login|auth|session)|web[\s_-]?api\s+(login|auth|session|token)|management\s+api\s+(login|auth|session)|login\s+request\s+(received|sent)|session\s+token\s+(issued|created|granted))</regex>
    <description>Check Point SmartConsole: management API authentication event on $(hostname) -- CVE-2026-16232 anchor (T1190)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>checkpoint_smartconsole_login,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1190 / T1078  - Auth bypass: success following prior failures
       Rule ID: 104153
       Classic bypass pattern: attacker fails once or twice (normal
       auth path rejected), then a crafted exploit request succeeds.
       Frequency: 1 success within 5 minutes of 3+ failures from
       the same source.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="104153" level="12" frequency="3" timeframe="300">
    <if_matched_sid>104152</if_matched_sid>
    <same_srcip/>
    <regex type="pcre2">(?i)(login\s+success|session\s+(token\s+)?(issued|created|granted|established)|authentication\s+success|authenticated\s+success|user\s+authenticated)</regex>
    <description>Check Point SmartConsole: authentication success from $(srcip) following 3+ recent login events on $(hostname) -- possible CVE-2026-16232 improper auth bypass; token may have been obtained without valid credentials (T1190, T1078)</description>
    <options>no_full_log</options>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
      <id>T1078</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>checkpoint_smartconsole_bypass,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1190  - Rapid SmartConsole login probes (exploit scanner)
       Rule ID: 104154
       Automated exploit tools or scanners probing the token endpoint
       will generate rapid sequential login requests. Frequency:
       6+ login events from the same source within 60 seconds.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="104154" level="12" frequency="6" timeframe="60">
    <if_matched_sid>104152</if_matched_sid>
    <same_srcip/>
    <description>Check Point SmartConsole: high-frequency login probes (6+ in 60s) from $(srcip) on $(hostname) -- automated CVE-2026-16232 exploit tool or token endpoint scanner detected (T1190)</description>
    <options>no_full_log</options>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>checkpoint_smartconsole_probe,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1190  - SmartConsole API authentication failures (recon)
       Rule ID: 104155
       Multiple auth failures from the same source indicate
       pre-exploitation reconnaissance or brute-force before
       CVE-2026-16232 bypass attempt. 5+ failures in 2 minutes.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="104155" level="11" frequency="5" timeframe="120">
    <program_name>^(api_server|cpmad|mgmtd|cpwmd|cpsmd)$</program_name>
    <regex type="pcre2">(?i)(login\s+fail|auth(entication)?\s+fail|invalid\s+(credentials|password|token)|unauthorized\s+(login|access)|session\s+(denied|rejected)|wrong\s+password|bad\s+credentials)</regex>
    <same_srcip/>
    <description>Check Point SmartConsole: repeated authentication failures (5+ in 2m) from $(srcip) on $(hostname) -- brute-force or CVE-2026-16232 pre-exploitation probe; investigate for follow-on token bypass (T1190)</description>
    <options>no_full_log</options>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>checkpoint_smartconsole_authfail,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1562.004  - Policy install/publish via SmartConsole (critical)
       Rule ID: 104156
       install-policy and publish are the highest-privilege API calls
       in SmartConsole - they push firewall rule changes to gateways.
       An attacker using CVE-2026-16232 bypass will often immediately
       run install-policy to create a permissive backdoor rule.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="104156" level="14">
    <program_name>^(api_server|cpmad|mgmtd|cpwmd|cpsmd)$</program_name>
    <regex type="pcre2">(?i)(install[\s_-]?policy|policy\s+install(ation)?|publish[\s_-]?session|session\s+published|policy\s+(pushed|deployed|applied|committed)|firewall\s+policy\s+(install|push|deploy))</regex>
    <description>Check Point SmartConsole: firewall policy install or publish operation on $(hostname) -- privileged API operation that pushes rules to managed gateways; correlate with CVE-2026-16232 bypass indicators for unauthorized policy modification (T1562.004, T1190)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1562.004</id>
      <id>T1190</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>checkpoint_policy_install,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1098  - Admin account creation via SmartConsole (persistence)
       Rule ID: 104157
       After bypassing authentication via CVE-2026-16232, attackers
       create a backdoor administrator account to maintain persistent
       access to the firewall management plane even after the token
       expires or the vulnerability is patched.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="104157" level="14">
    <program_name>^(api_server|cpmad|mgmtd|cpwmd|cpsmd)$</program_name>
    <regex type="pcre2">(?i)(add[\s_-]?admin(istrator)?|create[\s_-]?admin(istrator)?|set[\s_-]?admin(istrator)?|new\s+admin(istrator)?\s+(created|added)|admin(istrator)?\s+(account\s+)?(created|added|provisioned)|user\s+created.*admin|admin.*user\s+created)</regex>
    <description>Check Point SmartConsole: administrator account created or modified via management API on $(hostname) -- post-exploitation persistence tactic consistent with CVE-2026-16232 bypass; verify this was authorized (T1098, T1078)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1098</id>
      <id>T1078</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>checkpoint_admin_created,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1190 / T1078  - Off-hours SmartConsole management access
       Rule ID: 104158
       SmartConsole management should happen during business hours.
       Authentication events outside 07:00-20:00 are behavioral
       anomalies that warrant investigation, especially given active
       exploitation of CVE-2026-16232.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="104158" level="9">
    <program_name>^(api_server|cpmad|mgmtd|cpwmd|cpsmd)$</program_name>
    <regex type="pcre2">(?i)(login\s+success|session\s+(token\s+)?(issued|created|granted|established)|authentication\s+success|user\s+authenticated)</regex>
    <time>20:00 - 07:00</time>
    <description>Check Point SmartConsole: management API authentication success outside business hours on $(hostname) -- off-hours management access; triage against CVE-2026-16232 active exploitation campaign (T1190, T1078)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
      <id>T1078</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>checkpoint_smartconsole_offhours,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1562.004  - Firewall access rule modification
       Rule ID: 104159
       Adding, deleting, or modifying access rules in SmartConsole
       is a high-value post-exploitation action - attackers disable
       blocking rules or add permissive rules to enable lateral
       movement after CVE-2026-16232 bypass.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="104159" level="13">
    <program_name>^(api_server|cpmad|mgmtd|cpwmd|cpsmd)$</program_name>
    <regex type="pcre2">(?i)(add[\s_-]?access[\s_-]?rule|delete[\s_-]?access[\s_-]?rule|set[\s_-]?access[\s_-]?rule|access\s+rule\s+(added|deleted|modified|created|changed)|firewall\s+rule\s+(added|deleted|modified|created)|security\s+policy\s+(rule\s+)?(modified|changed|updated)|network\s+(object\s+)?(added|deleted|created|modified))</regex>
    <description>Check Point SmartConsole: firewall access rule or network object modification on $(hostname) -- policy change via management API; if correlated with CVE-2026-16232 indicators, attacker may be creating permissive rules for lateral movement (T1562.004)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1562.004</id>
      <id>T1190</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>checkpoint_rule_modified,</group>
  </rule>

</group>
